package servoimpl

// Contract1 is the runtime contract every file `servo generate` writes from
// v3.5.0 on names, as `const _ = servoimpl.Contract1`. A generated file is
// written against the servoimpl of the servo version that generated it,
// and the go.mod of the module it lands in may pin an older one; naming
// the contract makes that mismatch fail to compile on this one line, with
// the generated comment beside it saying which version the file needs,
// rather than inside a helper whose signature moved.
//
// A generator that comes to rely on runtime behaviour this servoimpl does
// not have adds Contract2, and emits that, beside this. No ContractN is
// ever removed within a major version, so a file generated by any v3
// release keeps compiling against every later one. These constants are
// the one part of servoimpl the compatibility promise covers.
const Contract1 = true
